From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 12:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: attribute radar events to the detecting band

mt7996_mcu_rx_radar_detected() calls ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw, NULL),
which marks every chanctx on the shared multi-band wiphy including 2.4 GHz.
Read mphy->chanctx once with READ_ONCE() and pass its ieee80211_chanctx_conf
so only the detecting band's channel context is marked radar-affected.

Origin: https://github.com/Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18
Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/mt7996/mcu.c b/mt7996/mcu.c
index 110e0b5..a96cd2b 100644
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -609,10 +609,19 @@ mt7996_mcu_rx_radar_detected(struct mt7996_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 						&dev->rdd2_chandef,
 						GFP_ATOMIC);
 	} else {
+		struct ieee80211_chanctx_conf *conf = NULL;
 		struct mt7996_phy *phy = mphy->priv;
+		struct mt76_chanctx *ctx;
+
+		/* Attribute radar to the detecting band only; read unguarded chanctx once. */
+		ctx = READ_ONCE(mphy->chanctx);
+		if (ctx)
+			conf = container_of((void *)ctx,
+					    struct ieee80211_chanctx_conf,
+					    drv_priv);
 
 		phy->rdd_tx_paused = true;
-		ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw, NULL);
+		ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw, conf);
 	}
 	dev->hw_pattern++;
 
